FenrirOS updates come from apk, not APT (pve-manager's PVE::API2::APT is
replaced by an apk version, files/APT.pm):
- the node's "Repositories" panel and the summary's repository status are
  removed: they manage Debian/Proxmox APT repository files
  (/etc/apk/repositories is not edited from the web UI);
- pveupgrade (the web UI's "Upgrade" console) runs "apk upgrade" instead of
  "apt-get dist-upgrade"; its "database out of date" check looks at the
  package list pveupdate writes (/var/lib/pve-manager/pkgupdates).
The "Updates" panel stays (it lists apk's upgradable packages).
Based on proxmox-nixos's pkgs/pve-manager/0001-no-apt-update.patch and
0002-no-repo-status.patch (which remove both panels); written for FenrirOS.

